WEBVTT

NOTE placeholder captions for V2 from the storyboard narration (temp)

V2-1-1
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:14.067
The funnel is made up of the actions that users, or potential customers, have to take.

V2-1-2
00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:22.000
It is the result of the marketing strategy, not a separate thing from it.

V2-2-1
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:22.581
Impression.

V2-2-2
00:00:22.581 --> 00:00:23.163
Engagement.

V2-2-3
00:00:23.163 --> 00:00:23.744
Action.

V2-2-4
00:00:23.744 --> 00:00:24.907
Goal fulfilled.

V2-2-5
00:00:24.907 --> 00:00:33.628
Some users leave the funnel with every extra click or action you ask of them.

V2-2-6
00:00:33.628 --> 00:00:42.349
Every extra step you add loses people, so a step has to earn its place.

V2-2-7
00:00:42.349 --> 00:00:47.000
If you need six sales, work it backwards.

V2-3-1
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.000
All traffic sources bring value.

V2-3-2
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.600
Every one of them.

V2-3-3
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:55.400
Every traffic source has a cost, including the ones that look free.

V2-3-4
00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.200
Content costs time and time costs money.

V2-3-5
00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:05.000
Operate by a clear economic model, or you cannot tell a good channel from a bad one.

V2-4-1
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:21.935
If a lead costs 30 dollars and one in five leads becomes a sale, a sale costs 150 dollars in marketing.

V2-4-2
00:01:21.935 --> 00:01:30.000
If the customer is worth 400 dollars, the channel works.
